<Docs title="Getting started" active="Getting started" description="Install agent-guard and authorize your first AI agent action.">
  <div class="doc-title"><span class="section-kicker">GUIDE / 01</span><h1>Getting started</h1><p>Get from zero to a verified authorization decision in five minutes.</p></div>
  <h2>Install the CLI</h2><p>agent-guard is self-hosted and Apache-2.0 licensed. Install from the repository while the project is in active development:</p><div class="doc-code">git clone https://github.com/sachncs/agent-guard.git<br />cd agent-guard<br />cargo install --path crates/agentguard-cli<br />cargo install --path crates/agentguard-server</div>
  <h2>Create a policy</h2><p>Initialize a project to create a Cedar schema and a starter policy directory.</p><div class="doc-code">mkdir my-agent<br />cd my-agent<br />agentguard init --name my-agent<br />agentguard validate</div>
  <h2>Narrow the starter permissions</h2><p>The generated policies grant broad development access to agents and the admin user. Replace the contents of both generated policy files before production. For this tutorial, leave 10_admin.cedar empty and put this rule in 20_agents.cedar:</p>
  <pre class="doc-code"><code>{'permit (principal == Agent::"research", action == Action::"ToolCall::repo_read", resource == Repository::"demo");'}</code></pre>
  <h2>Ask for a decision</h2><p>Save the following as request.json. This is the CLI request format; the HTTP endpoint uses the separate AuthZEN format described in the API reference.</p>
  <pre class="doc-code"><code>{JSON.stringify({principal:{type:"agent",uid:"research"},action:{tool:"repo_read"},resource:{entity_type:"Repository",uid:"demo",attrs:{org:"my-agent"}},context:{args:{repo:"demo"},session:{}}},null,2)}</code></pre>
  <div class="doc-code">agentguard validate<br />agentguard authorize request.json</div>
  <p>The matching request should allow. Change the principal UID to another agent and repeat; no permit matches, so the decision should deny. Only execute the real tool after receiving an allow.</p>
  <h2>Run the policy server</h2><p>For a language-agnostic deployment, run the AuthZEN-compatible server and point your agent middleware at it.</p><div class="doc-code">agentguard-server --listen tcp://127.0.0.1:8443</div>
  <div class="doc-next"><span>Next</span><a href="../concepts/">Understand the authorization model →</a></div>
</Docs>
